# claude-anvil configuration.
# Source this file (or export these vars) before launching Claude Code.
#   export $(grep -v '^#' .env | xargs)     # one-shot in a bash shell
#
# You do NOT need to set every variable. Only the reviewers whose env vars are
# set AND whose credentials/daemons are reachable will actually attack the diff.
# Unconfigured reviewers just write a "concern: not configured" stub to the
# ledger and the other reviewers continue.

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ledger location (SQLite file). Default: ~/.claude-anvil/anvil.db
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ANVIL_DB_PATH=~/.claude-anvil/anvil.db

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reviewer roster. Comma-separated. Valid ids: claude, openai, gemini, ollama.
# Medium tasks pick the first available from ANVIL_MEDIUM_REVIEWER.
# Large / 🔴 tasks pick the first three available from ANVIL_LARGE_REVIEWERS.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
ANVIL_MEDIUM_REVIEWER=claude
ANVIL_LARGE_REVIEWERS=claude,gemini,ollama

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per-reviewer on/off switch. Overrides `reviewers.<name>.enabled` in
# config.json (env always wins). Accepts true/1/yes/on and false/0/no/off.
# A disabled reviewer is dropped from both rosters and never called.
# Persist the same thing without env vars:
#     anvil-config.py disable openai      # keeps api_key/endpoint/model
#     anvil-config.py enable  openai
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ANVIL_CLAUDE_ENABLED=true
# ANVIL_OPENAI_ENABLED=false
# ANVIL_GEMINI_ENABLED=true
# ANVIL_OLLAMA_ENABLED=false

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Claude reviewer model. The Claude reviewer runs as a Task subagent, so this
# only selects the model; credentials come from your Claude Code session.
# Valid: sonnet, haiku, opus, or an explicit claude-* model id.
# The same value lives in plugin/agents/code-review-claude.md (line 5), which
# /anvil-setup rewrites; this env var overrides config.json for `validate claude`.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ANVIL_CLAUDE_MODEL=sonnet

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reviewer HTTP deadlines (seconds). Both are true wall-clock bounds, so a
# provider that stalls mid-response still returns control to /anvil instead of
# hanging the loop. Exceeding either yields a graceful stub verdict.
#   HTTP  = one request attempt
#   TOTAL = the whole call, covering all retries and backoff sleeps
# Lower these if you point a reviewer at a queued free-tier endpoint.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ANVIL_REVIEW_HTTP_TIMEOUT=180
# ANVIL_REVIEW_TOTAL_TIMEOUT=420

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OpenAI-compatible reviewer (OpenAI, Azure OpenAI, OpenRouter, Groq, ...)
# No free tier for gpt-4o on openai.com; free alternatives:
#   - OpenRouter free tier:
#       ANVIL_OPENAI_ENDPOINT=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions
#       ANVIL_OPENAI_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b:free
#   - Groq:
#       ANVIL_OPENAI_ENDPOINT=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1/chat/completions
#       ANVIL_OPENAI_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ANVIL_OPENAI_ENDPOINT=https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions
# ANVIL_OPENAI_API_KEY=
# ANVIL_OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o
# gpt-4o and o1/o3 only accept temperature=1 (o-series), so anvil auto-omits
# the field for o1/o3 models. For other models it sends temperature=0.2.
#
# Set to `off` if your endpoint (e.g. free OpenRouter / Groq models) rejects
# response_format: {type: json_object}. anvil-review.py still extracts JSON
# from fenced code blocks when strict JSON mode is off.
# ANVIL_OPENAI_JSON_MODE=on

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Gemini. Generous free tier at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ANVIL_GEMINI_API_KEY=
# ANVIL_GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash
# ANVIL_GEMINI_ENDPOINT=   # optional override; derived from model by default

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ollama (local, free). Install: https://ollama.com/download
# Recommended models for code review: qwen2.5-coder:14b, deepseek-coder-v2:16b
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ANVIL_OLLAMA_HOST=http://localhost:11434
# ANVIL_OLLAMA_MODEL=qwen2.5-coder:7b

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Caveman output mode. Compresses /anvil's free-form prose (~75%) while leaving
# Anvil's structured artifacts (Evidence Bundle, callouts, code, commits) intact.
# Valid levels: lite, full, ultra, wenyan-lite, wenyan-full, wenyan-ultra.
# Use off / none / disabled / empty to disable. Env wins over config.json.
# Default (unset) = off.
# Takes effect only if the separate `caveman` skill is installed (not bundled
# with claude-anvil); otherwise /anvil runs normal prose regardless of level.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ANVIL_CAVEMAN_LEVEL=off
